{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Eightfold.G2FrameDimensions","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Eightfold.G2FrameDimensions","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Nat.Choose.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.IntervalCases","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.NormNum","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Linarith","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring"],"declarations":17,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.G2Frame.choose_three_eq_one_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.G2Frame.choose_three_eq_one_iff","kind":"theorem","line":273,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/G2FrameDimensions.lean#L273-L285","doc":"**`Λᵏ` of a 3-dimensional object is a line iff `k = 0` or `k = 3`.**\n`C(3,k) = 1 ↔ k ∈ {0,3}`. So `Λ³W ≅ 𝟙` is the *only* non-trivial volume form a\nrank-3 object admits — the degree-3 half of the dichotomy in\n`QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.VolumeFormDegree`, at the dimension the\n`G₂/SU(3)` isotropy supplies (`6 = 2 · 3` real, i.e. complex 3). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.G2Frame.so_dim_eq_two_su2_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.G2Frame.so_dim_eq_two_su2_iff","kind":"theorem","line":255,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/G2FrameDimensions.lean#L255-L269","doc":"**`𝔰𝔬(4) ≅ 𝔰𝔲(2) ⊕ 𝔰𝔲(2)` at the level of dimensions, and only at `n = 4`.**\n`C(n,2) = 3 + 3` iff `n = 4`. This is where the tetraplectic `SU(2)` of\n`lem:bring-cone-reeb-quaternionic-twist` enters `G₂`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.G2Frame.no_unitary_quotient_of_dim_eight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.G2Frame.no_unitary_quotient_of_dim_eight","kind":"theorem","line":240,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/G2FrameDimensions.lean#L240-L253","doc":"**No unitary subgroup gives an 8-dimensional `G₂` quotient.**\n`14 − (n² − 1) = 8` would need `n² = 7`. The mirror of\n`no_orthogonal_quotient_of_dim_six`: the Wolf space is not `G₂/SU(n)` for any `n`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.G2Frame.no_orthogonal_quotient_of_dim_six","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.G2Frame.no_orthogonal_quotient_of_dim_six","kind":"theorem","line":226,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/G2FrameDimensions.lean#L226-L238","doc":"**No orthogonal subgroup gives a 6-dimensional `G₂` quotient — at all.**\n`C(n,2)` jumps `6 → 10` from `n = 4` to `n = 5`, so `14 − C(n,2)` never equals `6`.\nConsequence for the framework: `S⁶` is *not* reachable from the orthogonal series,\nso the tetraplectic `SU(2)` leg — which enters `G₂` through `SO(4)` — cannot be\ndeformed into the colour leg by any change of `n`. The two fragments meet in `G₂`\nand nowhere below it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.G2Frame.g2_quotient_so_dim_eight_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.G2Frame.g2_quotient_so_dim_eight_iff","kind":"theorem","line":212,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/G2FrameDimensions.lean#L212-L224","doc":"**`SO(4)` is the only orthogonal subgroup with an 8-dimensional `G₂`\nquotient.** `14 − dim 𝔰𝔬(n) = 8` iff `n = 4`. The quotient is the quaternionic\nWolf space `G₂/SO(4)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.G2Frame.g2_quotient_su_dim_six_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.G2Frame.g2_quotient_su_dim_six_iff","kind":"theorem","line":195,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/G2FrameDimensions.lean#L195-L210","doc":"**`SU(3)` is the only unitary subgroup with a 6-dimensional `G₂` quotient.**\n`14 − dim 𝔰𝔲(n) = 6` iff `n = 3`. The quotient is `S⁶`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.G2Frame.sq_sub_choose_three_eq_g2_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.G2Frame.sq_sub_choose_three_eq_g2_iff","kind":"theorem","line":177,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/G2FrameDimensions.lean#L177-L191","doc":"**Dimension 7 is the unique one whose generic-3-form stabiliser has dimension\n`dim 𝔤₂`.** If the `GL(n)` orbit of a 3-form is open then the stabiliser has\ndimension `n² − C(n,3)`, and that equals `14` for `n = 7` and for no other `n`.\nThe classical fact that the stabiliser there is `G₂` is input, not proved here;\nwhat is proved is that the arithmetic leaves exactly one candidate dimension. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.G2Frame.choose_four_le_sq_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.G2Frame.choose_four_le_sq_iff","kind":"theorem","line":163,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/G2FrameDimensions.lean#L163-L175","doc":"**4-forms: the count permits an open orbit exactly for `n ≤ 7`.** So the first\nfailure is `n = 8`: `C(8,4) = 70 > 64 = dim GL(8)`. This is bean `qou-8p1f`'s\nnegative — \"no 4-form on `ℝ⁸` has an open orbit, so *generic 4-form* singles out\nnothing\" — with the surrounding series supplied, which is what shows `8` is a\nboundary rather than an isolated bad case. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.G2Frame.choose_three_le_sq_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.G2Frame.choose_three_le_sq_iff","kind":"theorem","line":152,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/G2FrameDimensions.lean#L152-L161","doc":"**3-forms: the count permits an open orbit exactly for `n ≤ 8`.**\n`C(7,3) = 35 ≤ 49` and `C(8,3) = 56 ≤ 64`, but `C(9,3) = 84 > 81`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.G2Frame.sq_lt_choose_four_of_eight_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.G2Frame.sq_lt_choose_four_of_eight_le","kind":"theorem","line":142,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/G2FrameDimensions.lean#L142-L145","doc":"`n² < C(n,4)` for every `n ≥ 8`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.G2Frame.sq_lt_choose_three_of_nine_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.G2Frame.sq_lt_choose_three_of_nine_le","kind":"theorem","line":137,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/G2FrameDimensions.lean#L137-L140","doc":"`n² < C(n,3)` for every `n ≥ 9`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.G2Frame.sq_lt_choose_succ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.G2Frame.sq_lt_choose_succ","kind":"theorem","line":121,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/G2FrameDimensions.lean#L121-L135","doc":"**The induction that makes `C(n,k+1)` outrun `n²`.** If the inequality holds at\n`n₀` and each step of `C(·,k)` exceeds the increment `2m + 1` of a square, it holds\nfrom `n₀` on. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.G2Frame.two_mul_add_one_le_choose_three","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.G2Frame.two_mul_add_one_le_choose_three","kind":"theorem","line":111,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/G2FrameDimensions.lean#L111-L119","doc":"`2n + 1 ≤ C(n,3)` for `n ≥ 6`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.G2Frame.two_mul_add_one_le_choose_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.G2Frame.two_mul_add_one_le_choose_two","kind":"theorem","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/G2FrameDimensions.lean#L100-L109","doc":"`2n + 1 ≤ C(n,2)` for `n ≥ 6`. The step needed to beat the increment of a\nsquare. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.G2Frame.dimG2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.G2Frame.dimG2","kind":"def","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/G2FrameDimensions.lean#L93-L96","doc":"`dim 𝔤₂ = 14`. Proved for `Der(𝕆)` over `ℚ` in\n`QOU.MathlibExt.OctonionDerivations.octonion_derivation_dim`; used here as a\nnumeral. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.G2Frame.dimSO","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.G2Frame.dimSO","kind":"def","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/G2FrameDimensions.lean#L90-L91","doc":"`dim 𝔰𝔬(n) = C(n,2)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.G2Frame.dimSU","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.G2Frame.dimSU","kind":"def","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/G2FrameDimensions.lean#L87-L88","doc":"`dim 𝔰𝔲(n) = n² − 1`. A naming function on `ℕ`, not a group. ","signatureChunk":0}]}